    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 210354\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n854 PM PDT Sun Sep 20 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* Dry and seasonable conditions will give way to increased \n  precipitation chances and a relative cool down on Monday and \n  Tuesday.\n\n* Temperatures will recover during the second half of the week\n  with low precipitation chances returning for northwest Arizona\n  as we head into the weekend.\n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...through Sunday. \n\nPlenty of high clouds streaming into the area today ahead of an \nupper low off the central California coast. This low will move \nonshore tomorrow and provide the chance of showers and\nthunderstorms (30 to 60%) to much of the region but will favor \nInyo County and the southern Great Basin. This convective activity\nmay continue well into the evening across Lincoln County. \nInstability will be somewhat limited, generally, 100-300 J/kg. \nTemperatures will cool marginally behind the low on Tuesday with \nmost locations 3 to 6 degrees cooler than high temperatures that \nwe will see today. The low will eject fairly quickly to the \nnortheast on Tuesday morning but there may be a few lingering \nshowers into the early afternoon in Lincoln County. \n\nGenerally, dry southwesterly flow will be in place for the rest of \nthe week and into next weekend. The exception to this is with the \nensemble guidance hinting towards a modest uptick in moisture \nmainly south and east of Las Vegas on Thursday and Friday. \nCurrently, the best chances of precipitation associated with this \nmoisture are around 10 to 20 percent in Mohave County. \nTemperatures will be around their seasonal normals on Wednesday \nand increase a few degrees on Thursday and remain fairly flat into\nthe weekend. \n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 06Z Forecast Package...Winds \ngenerally follow typical daily directional patterns with speeds \nunder 10 knots. However, southeasterly winds on Monday afternoon \nincrease to around 10 knots with gusts between 15 and 18 knots. \nAfter sunset, winds shift back to the southwest and fall to under 10 \nknots. Cannot rule out another northerly push of winds on Monday \nnight due to outflow from the northwest. Mid and high cloud cover \nwill increase throughout the day, with bases at or above 15kft. \nShowers are possible over the mountains surrounding the Las Vegas \nValley during the afternoon and evening, but these are not expected \nto reach the terminal.\n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast\nCalifornia...For the 06Z Forecast Package...Winds should be light \nand variable for most of the area tonight. One exception is the \nwestern Mojave Desert including KDAG, where westerly winds over 10 \nknots persist. Elevated southeasterly winds with gusts between 15 \nand 25 knots pick across most of the area during the afternoon, \nlasting through sunset. At the same time, southerly winds with gusts \nto around 20 knots pick up at KBIH and westerly winds of around 10 \nknots will continue at KDAG. Cloud cover will increase through the \nday with bases at or above 10kft. Showers and thunderstorms develop \nover high terrain of Inyo County, some of which may reach KBIH. \n\n&&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Czyzyk\nAVIATION...Meltzer\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
